      * Second in-program suite: the MAIN paragraph of LEGACY gathers
      * the hardest cases for the rewriter (statements closed only by
      * the period, nested phrases, IF/ELSE IF, inline PERFORM, indexed
      * file, dynamic CALL, clock). It is the regression of the parser.
       TESTSUITE TSTLEG 'Legacy (in-program on LEGACY)'
       PROGRAM LEGACY

       BEFORE-EACH
           MOVE ZERO TO WS-B
           MOVE SPACES TO WS-GRP WS-TIME
           MOVE "N" TO END-OF-FILE
       END-BEFORE

       TESTCASE 'main fully mocked: the original does not run'
           MOCK PARAGRAPH MAIN
               MOVE 7 TO WS-B
           END-MOCK
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 7
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH MAIN HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY OPEN MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'original main with file, dynamic CALL and clock mocked'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "K001" TO M-KEY
                   MOVE SPACES TO M-DATA
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               MOVE 1 TO WS-B
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '12345678'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE 'K001'
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 4
           EXPECT WS-TIME TO BE '12345678'
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '00'
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'N'
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH MAIN HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG NEVER HAPPENED
           VERIFY CLOCK HAPPENED 3 TIMES
           VERIFY READ MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY START MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY DELETE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY OPEN MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CLOSE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'CALL path: the key matches and the mock adds'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ
                   MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
               EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE 'XXXX'
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
      * WS-B: 1 for the key, +1 from NOT ON EXCEPTION of the mocked CALL
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 2
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED

       TESTCASE 'invalid read: INVALID KEY of the original'
           MOCK FILE MASTER-FILE
               ON READ AT END
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT END-OF-FILE TO BE 'Y'
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '00'
           VERIFY READ MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE

      * The next two tests do not mock MASTER-FILE: they use the real
      * indexed file (build/master.dat), which each case leaves with a
      * single record of key "XXXX", to reach the INVALID KEY clauses of
      * WRITE, REWRITE, START and DELETE, which a mock cannot trigger.
       TESTCASE 'duplicate key: WRITE and START take INVALID KEY'
           OPEN OUTPUT MASTER-FILE
           MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
           MOVE SPACES TO M-DATA
           WRITE M-REC
           CLOSE MASTER-FILE
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
      * the called program leaves WS-B at 0; the NOT ON EXCEPTION (which
      * GnuCOBOL binds to the preceding DISPLAY, not to the CALL) raises
      * it to 1 and MAIN takes WHEN 1: WRITE with the key that exists
               MOVE 0 TO WS-B
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
      * the WRITE repeats the key and START finds no greater one, so
      * MAIN jumps to EXIT-PARA with no DELETE or CLOSE. THRU keeps that
      * GO TO inside the range of the PERFORM; with a bare PERFORM MAIN
      * the flow would fall off the end of the program and Cobalto would
      * report it as a failure of the case.
           PERFORM MAIN THRU EXIT-PARA
           EXPECT WS-KEY TO BE 'XXXX'
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 1
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '23'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY WRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH EXIT-PARA HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY DELETE MASTER-FILE NEVER HAPPENED
           CLOSE MASTER-FILE

       TESTCASE 'changed key: REWRITE and DELETE take INVALID KEY'
           OPEN OUTPUT MASTER-FILE
           MOVE "XXXX" TO M-KEY
           MOVE SPACES TO M-DATA
           WRITE M-REC
           CLOSE MASTER-FILE
           MOCK CALL WS-PROG
      * the called program changes the key of the record just read: the
      * REWRITE no longer finds it, START does find a greater one and
      * the DELETE does not find it either
               MOVE "AAAA" TO M-KEY
           END-MOCK
           MOCK CLOCK
               TIME '00000000'
           END-MOCK
           PERFORM MAIN
           EXPECT WS-B TO BE NUMERIC 2
      * the "E" left by the REWRITE is overwritten by the START, the
      * DELETE and the CLOSE: the proof of the path is branch coverage
           EXPECT WS-FS TO BE '00'
           VERIFY CALL WS-PROG HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY REWRITE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY DELETE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY CLOSE MASTER-FILE HAPPENED ONCE
           VERIFY PARAGRAPH EXIT-PARA NEVER HAPPENED
